course: dictionary
lesson: 9292
title: One word, three meanings: spawn
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words wear more than one coat. Spawn can be a verb (something you do) or a noun (a thing). Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits. «In March a garden pond can fill with clumps of jelly dotted with black eggs: common frog spawn.» Here spawn is a thing: the jelly full of eggs.
explain: Now look at the verb. «Salmon swim upriver to spawn.» Spawn is something the fish do. Ask yourself: what would fit in the gap? They swim upriver to lay eggs. That fits, so spawn means to lay eggs in water.
explain: Sometimes spawn means something new is made. «The film spawned three sequels.» A film cannot lay eggs, so the clue is the sequels. The film caused new films to appear. Gamers use it too: a player spawns when they appear in the game world.
fact: Spawn can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action).
fact: «Frog spawn» means the clump of eggs that frogs lay in water.
fact: One common frog can lay about 1,000 to 2,000 eggs.
fact: Each frogspawn egg sits in its own jelly ball, which protects it and keeps it warm.
fact: In games, the spawn point is the place where a player or character appears.
exercise: «In March a garden pond can fill with clumps of jelly dotted with black eggs.» What is the jelly with black eggs called? | Duckweed | *Frog spawn | Pond weed | Tadpoles
exercise: «Common frog spawn comes in a clump, each egg in its own jelly ball that protects it and keeps it warm.» What does the jelly do? | It makes the pond smell sweet | It keeps the eggs cold and dry | *It protects each egg and keeps it warm | It turns the eggs into tadpoles at once
exercise: «The film spawned three sequels.» What does spawned mean here? | Watched by three children | Lost three scenes | *Caused three new films to appear | Filmed in three places
test: «Salmon swim upriver to spawn.» What does spawn mean here? | To swim very fast | To sleep under rocks | *To lay eggs in the water | To hunt for food
test: In a video game, a player spawns back into the game after losing a life. What does spawns mean? | Turns the screen off | *Appears again in the game world | Stops playing for good | Runs away from the game
exam: «A small pond without fish invites frogs, because fish eat spawn and tadpoles.» Why is a pond without fish good for frogs? | *Fish would eat their spawn and tadpoles | Fish make the water too cold | Frogs like to be alone | Frogs cannot swim in water with fish
